extraction_notes: |
  - Book: Rifts World Book 12: Psyscape, printed 135 (R.C.C. heading and Special R.C.C.
    Abilities 1), 136 (full-page art, no text; cache p137 is empty), 137 (abilities 1-7 and the
    NPC Villain & Optional Player Character stat block), 138 (Weight, and "Notes about the
    Hatchling R.C.C." pointing to Rifts RPG page 97).
  - The stat block is headed NPC Villain & Optional Player Character AS A HATCHLING, and its
    Player Note says any player character is a first-level hatchling. Only the hatchling is
    stored as the playable class, modelled on production''s dragon-hatchling. Adult figures are
    in GM Notes and are not stored as a variant.
  - xp_table: none written. Printed 157 says the Zaayr uses the Dragon R.C.C.''s table, and
    production''s dragon-hatchling stores no xp_table.
  - men_of_arms: false. A race; the page states M.D.C. (mdc_base) but the key is written as the
    race default for consistency with the batch convention.
  - Psionics "either all Sensitive or all Healing" is a choose-1 special ability (the psi-pony
    shape), each option carrying its own psionics block. "All" was enumerated by name from the
    live catalog''s Rifts rows on 2026-09-25: rows whose system is heroes-unlimited or nightbane
    (Calm Rage, Wound Transfer, Induce Pain, Mimic Skills, Precognition, Sensory Link,
    Divination, Mediumship/Clairsentience) and the two Palladium Fantasy Main Book rows
    (Attack Disease, Transfer I.S.P.) were left out as not Rifts powers. A later Rifts
    Sensitive/Healing import will not reach this list by itself.
  - The per-level power from the other category and the Super-Psionic power every three levels
    are written as powers_schedule entries through level 15 (a schedule replaces a flat
    powers_per_level, so both are in the schedule).
  - I.S.P. "M.E. attribute number x5 plus 2D6+2 per level"; the adult +100 is GM Notes.
  - P.P.E. (Hatchling) "P.E. attribute number x10; does not increase with experience".
  - Magic: the page gives a repertoire ("limited to all light (not fire) and darkness spells
    plus Invisibility (Simple and Superior), Close Rift, and Dimensional Portal") and no
    starting count. Production''s dragon-hatchling grants no spells at creation, so no magic
    block is written; the repertoire is prose in the Magic Abilities special ability.
  - R.C.C. skills: "literate in Dragonese and one additional language" with no percentage;
    stored at 98% with no per-level gain (Literacy: Dragonese/Elven and Literacy: Other), matching the production dragon-hatchling, which stores its own unprinted literacy at 98%. Basic
    math is +20% (45 + 20 = 65). Advanced math is printed at a flat 98%.
  - Related picks: "any category except Cowboy, Medical, Military, Physical, Piloting, and
    Science". Piloting read as the Pilot category only; Pilot Related left in. The book prints
    no later skill picks, so no schedule.
  - Combat: "Equal to hand to hand: basic, +1 melee attack", stored as Hand to Hand: Basic plus
    bonuses.combat.attacks 1, as production''s dragon-hatchling does. No bonuses beyond
    attribute and skill bonuses for a hatchling. No upgrade price is printed, so no
    hand_to_hand block.
  - Horror/Awe Factor (Hatchling) 10 stored as horror_factor; adult 17 is GM Notes.
  - Not stored as numbers: supernatural P.S. (prose), eye laser and flame breath damage per level
    (prose), teleport percentages (prose), alignment tendencies (GM Notes).
  - Cache digit faults read against a render of printed 137: "!D6xlOO" is 1D6x100,
    "!D6xlOOO" is 1D6x1000, "!D4xlO" is 1D4x10, "2D6xlO" is 2D6x10.
